  "source": "r/GAMSAT GEMSAS interview & offer data (community-compiled)",
  "attribution": "Cutoffs blended from two community-compiled GEMSAS workbooks (2025 and 2024 application cycles) plus a third community dataset (screenshot-extracted, non-rural interview offers). p90 thresholds further validated and updated against two rejection datasets (700 unsuccessful applicants across all universities, 2025-2026 cycles). Rough guidance only, not official admissions data.",
  "notes": "interviewMin and p50 derived from observed interview pools; p90 validated against rejection data (rejection max and P95 per university/cohort). p90 is set above the 95th percentile of rejection scores so that fewer than 5% of rejections exceed it. UWA nonRural max-rejection outlier (1.833, GPA=7 GAMSAT=83) and UQ rural outlier excluded as anomalous pathway data. Bonuses modelled in calculator: MQ applies +3% per eligible cohort (rural/indigenous/MQ Clinical grad) capped at 5%, applied to raw GPA before combo. Deakin bonuses are additive to the final combo score (deakinGrad +4%, ahpraClinical +4%, workExp +2%, financialDisadvantage +2%, ruralRegional 0-4%) capped at 12% total; ahpraClinical and workExp are mutually exclusive. UQ adjusts GPA: PhD/MPhil/Honours I sets GPA to 7.0; Masters by Research adds 0.2; Honours IIA/IIB/III use midpoints of published ranges (6.75/5.75/4.5). Deakin rural tier breakdown is not publicly documented; users must enter their tier manually. Scores are on the GEMSAS combo scale (GPA/7 + GAMSAT_weighted/100).",
